Whoa.

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:04.090
- [Jackson] SpaghettiOs

00:00:04.090 --> 00:00:04.923
- All right.

00:00:04.923 --> 00:00:07.060
Jackson asked to make pretzels

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:08.000
Mm!

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.310
- [Jackson] And the trailer.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:10.300
- [Hannah] Yes!

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:11.133
- [Jackson] Sour.

00:00:11.133 --> 00:00:12.000
- [Wyatt] Grass pizza.

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:15.740
- [Hannah] It was truly one
of the most beautiful days

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.913
we've had it a very long time.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.170
Hi, I'm Hannah.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:21.510
I'm the world's OK-est mom

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:24.810
and I have been really boring
and tired this past year.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.240
It's true. I been very overwhelmed.

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.980
I've been on autopilot and
I've been really tired.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:34.980
And so I want to kind of
reinvigorate the fun in our family.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.600
I'm bringing back an old video.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.650
A very long time ago, I only
said yes to my kids for a week.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:42.560
At the time they were very young

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.510
and I want to see what it looks
like now that they're older.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:48.530
So, for one week, I'm going
to only say yes to my kids

00:00:48.530 --> 00:00:50.640
to everything they ask for. Wish me luck.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.640
So here's the plan.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.990
I really don't want
them to catch onto this

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:55.550
because I don't want their requests

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:58.980
to snowball and escalate
into something I can't do.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:03.120
But, my hope is that it creates
some fun, memorable moments

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.480
for us and also new ways
for us to bond together.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:08.040
The rules pretty much stay the same

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:10.390
as the last time we did
this. It's gotta be a secret.

00:01:10.390 --> 00:01:12.320
They can't find out that I'm doing this.

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.560
We got to keep it clean.

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.640
They have to bathe, they
have to brush their teeth.

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.300
They have to do personal hygiene.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:19.500
But the little addition
this time around is it

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.000
has to be pandemic friendly.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:23.300
We can't be planning
things that aren't safe.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:27.110
We're taking our walk, our
usual neighborhood walk.

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:30.130
Whoa, almost hit me.

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:33.010
The first thing the boys asked
for was surprisingly easy

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:34.960
which I was not expecting.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.150
They asked if we could
take our neighborhood

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.513
walk that we like to take.

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:40.963
Nice.

00:01:41.940 --> 00:01:44.560
Of course the first thing
they asked for isn't crazy

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:46.330
because they have no idea what's going on.

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.420
So, I really should have known

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.440
that it would have been an average day

00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:53.540
for that first day of me trying this.

00:01:53.540 --> 00:01:55.580
So here's hoping it will stay this way

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:57.100
for the rest of the week.

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:58.480
It really didn't take long

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.386
for the weird food requests
to start coming in.

00:02:01.386 --> 00:02:02.219
- SpaghettiOs

00:02:02.219 --> 00:02:07.219
- [Hannah] You want
SpaghettiOs for lunch at 10 30?

00:02:07.389 --> 00:02:08.222
- Yeah

00:02:08.222 --> 00:02:09.055
- [Hannah] Okay.

00:02:09.055 --> 00:02:09.888
- They're so good.

00:02:09.888 --> 00:02:10.721
- [Hannah] Go ahead.

00:02:10.721 --> 00:02:12.150
- They're so good.

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:14.530
- Wyatt has always been
really difficult at mealtime.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:16.750
He doesn't like sitting down for meals.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:20.200
He doesn't like finishing
all the food on his plate.

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:24.510
So this actually clued me
into maybe his hunger pattern

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:27.590
is a little bit different
than my meal schedule.

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.000
And I might need to adjust a
little bit for him to make sure

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.580
that he's eating enough
and also enjoying his food.

00:02:34.580 --> 00:02:36.350
As a parent, I'm always learning.

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:39.530
And so that taught me a
little bit more about Wyatt.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.680
- Jackson asked to make pretzels

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:44.900
homemade soft pretzels today.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:46.549
I would have never said yes to this.

00:02:46.549 --> 00:02:48.570
They take forever to make.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.700
But, I had to say yes.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:51.189
What do we have here Jackson?

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:55.128
- We have yeast, sugar, salt and water.

00:02:55.128 --> 00:02:56.430
- [Hannah] And then what is this?

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:57.909
- [Jackson] Flour.

00:02:57.909 --> 00:03:00.470
- Yep. Our dough is coming together.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.730
Give it a slap.

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:05.163
Like this, there we go. This
a little fat boy pretzel.

00:03:07.106 --> 00:03:08.490
- I do this.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:09.407
- [Hannah] Give it a try.

00:03:09.407 --> 00:03:10.240
- Twist it.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.232
- [Hannah] Careful not to `drop it.

00:03:12.232 --> 00:03:14.734
(Hannah and Matt laughing)

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:16.240
Look at that!

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:18.400
This thick boy. Oh my gosh,

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.630
I did not feel like making these at all.

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:24.264
I'm so glad we did. They smell fantastic.

00:03:24.264 --> 00:03:25.097
Mm!

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:27.713
They were a little fluffy.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:29.977
- Amazing.

00:03:29.977 --> 00:03:31.440
- [Hannah] Did you guys do a good job?

00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:32.273
- Mhm.

00:03:32.273 --> 00:03:33.721
- [Hannah] What do you want Henry?

00:03:33.721 --> 00:03:35.587
(Henry cries)

00:03:35.587 --> 00:03:37.600
You want me to hold you? Okay.

00:03:37.600 --> 00:03:40.193
Even Henry gets yes.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.133
Are you happy now?

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:42.980
- Mama.

00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:43.813
- Baby.

00:03:43.813 --> 00:03:44.646
(baby talks)

00:03:44.646 --> 00:03:47.130
Yep. By day three, I'm
pretty sure the boys

00:03:47.130 --> 00:03:48.670
were catching on because they asked me

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.280
for something I would never agree to do.

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:53.560
All right. What did you ask me to make?

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:57.420
- I asked you to make
a yummy candy platter.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:01.400
- Candy platter. All
right. Let's get started.

00:04:01.400 --> 00:04:02.233
- Yeah!

00:04:02.233 --> 00:04:03.500
- I love candy TikTok.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:07.350
So, there are all these
amazing candy shops on TikTok.

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:10.760
With these cool candies that
just looked so fun to eat

00:04:10.760 --> 00:04:12.530
